{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01494",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.74,
      "end_seconds": 4.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.33,
      "end_seconds": 12.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 16.11,
      "end_seconds": 20.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.63,
      "end_seconds": 25.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a dry cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 26.63,
      "end_seconds": 40.84,
      "duration_seconds": 14.21,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Respiratory rate 21, height 164 centimetres. Weight 93 kilos, BMI works out to 34.6, heart rate 91, oxygen saturation is 93 percent, BP is 130 over 88."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.77,
      "end_seconds": 45.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.28,
      "end_seconds": 48.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "It comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.49,
      "end_seconds": 52.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "What eases it, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.7,
      "end_seconds": 55.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Honey helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.62,
      "end_seconds": 61.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.01,
      "end_seconds": 83.25,
      "duration_seconds": 21.24,
      "text": "A four out of ten, I suppose. And loss of taste, too. Mm, about loss of taste, it feels moderate to me. I've also been feeling short of breath. About feeling short of breath, I'd say once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.85,
      "end_seconds": 87.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Did you get blue lips or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.27,
      "end_seconds": 91.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.0,
      "end_seconds": 95.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Did you get vomiting, diarrhoea or confusion?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.46,
      "end_seconds": 103.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Uh, no vomiting, diarrhoea or confusion, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.9,
      "end_seconds": 106.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Nothing like chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.91,
      "end_seconds": 112.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "I haven't noticed any chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.51,
      "end_seconds": 116.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "So, any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.38,
      "end_seconds": 118.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.99,
      "end_seconds": 122.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.71,
      "end_seconds": 128.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "My father had bowel cancer. My aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.65,
      "end_seconds": 135.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.51,
      "end_seconds": 141.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.89,
      "end_seconds": 148.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "So, what do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.14,
      "end_seconds": 153.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.51,
      "end_seconds": 158.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.78,
      "end_seconds": 167.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.44,
      "text": "I, I take hydrochlorothiazide, 12.5 milligrams, maybe, every morning for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.2,
      "end_seconds": 171.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.01,
      "end_seconds": 187.77,
      "duration_seconds": 14.76,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Dolo, 650 milligrams, when I get the fever. I, I was on metoprolol before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.56,
      "end_seconds": 192.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.03,
      "end_seconds": 209.61,
      "duration_seconds": 13.58,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.37,
      "end_seconds": 214.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.01,
      "end_seconds": 217.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Diabetes, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.18,
      "end_seconds": 220.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.94,
      "end_seconds": 223.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.62,
      "end_seconds": 226.46,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.75,
      "end_seconds": 231.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Alright, diabetes, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.01,
      "end_seconds": 253.07,
      "duration_seconds": 12.06,
      "text": "So, based on your history, I don't have a clear answer today: a viral chest infection with mildly low oxygen is possible, and so is a flare of heart failure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.06,
      "end_seconds": 257.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.77,
      "end_seconds": 280.58,
      "duration_seconds": 18.81,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a viral chest infection with mildly low oxygen do well once it's treated properly. Just to be sure I understood. You've had a dry cough, and no diarrhoea or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.54,
      "end_seconds": 284.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 301.04,
      "end_seconds": 305.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "We've already done a viral swab this morning, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.5,
      "end_seconds": 313.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Thanks, that helps. I'm sending you for a chest X-ray because of low oxygen and crackles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.21,
      "end_seconds": 316.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "When would that take place?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.11,
      "end_seconds": 341.87,
      "duration_seconds": 23.76,
      "text": "Rest, keep your fluids up and lie on your tummy or side to help your breathing. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Let's plan a check in two days. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.65,
      "end_seconds": 346.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}